\((-6,-0.4)\) & Controlled \\
\((-7,-1.3)\) & Controlled \\
\((-4,-1.4)\) & Controlled \\
\((-5,-0.6)\) & Controlled \\
\((-9,-1.9)\) & Uncontrolled \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

Four trajectories approached the stable node, while two
escaped. Therefore, even when a stable equilibrium exists,
control still depends on the initial condition.

